Q: onBlur firing before onChange when selecting from dropdown - value not saved A: <p>You need to <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/blur_event#event_delegation" rel="nofollow noreferrer">handle the blur event in the capturing phase, instead of bubbling phase</a> (default) so <code>WidgetInlineEditField</code> can capture the <code>focus</code> event triggered by clicking <code>TimeInput</code>  which wouldn't meet the condition to trigger <code>handleCancel()</code> .</p>
<p>In TSX you would replace <code>onBlur</code>  with <code>onBlurCapture</code> :</p>
<pre class="lang-tsx prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div
    onBlurCapture={(e): void =&gt; { // Capture fires before onBlur
        if (!e.currentTarget.contains(e.relatedTarget)) {
          handleCancel();
        }
      }
    }
&gt;
  {edit ? children : readValue}
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>In Typescript you would add <code>true</code> as the second parameter, <code>useCapture</code>, of <code>addEventEventListener</code>  like:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>element.addEventListener((e): void =&gt; {
    if (!e.currentTarget.contains(e.relatedTarget)) {
        handleCancel();
    }
  }
}, true) // useCapture 
</code></pre>

Q: Flexbox CSS not stacking? A: <p>Add <code>min-width: 200px;</code> to the class <code>.col</code> .</p>
<p>It forces the <code>.col</code> element to wrap if it reached the selected width, and you can edit the number in <code>min-width</code> selector to tell when it should wrap (Become in column) and not be squeezed. Here's the entire code edited (With other improvements to make the cols have auto width in vertical mode, like making the <code>flex-direction: column</code> in <code>.row</code> on <code>@media</code>):</p>
